  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Cyclophosphamide is an alkylating anticancer drug used to treat many cancers, including breast and ovarian cancer, leukemias, and lymphomas, as well as several autoimmune diseases such as lupus and vasculitis. It is an approved medicine and appears on the WHO list of essential medicines, so it is widely used worldwide.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q408524&quot;>Wikidata Q408524</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>cyclophosphamide</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>L01AA01</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00531&quot;>DB00531</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/2907&quot;>2907</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:4027&quot;>4027</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q408524&quot;>Q408524</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C7H15Cl2N2O2P</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>261.083 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
